Some More Suggestions for the Next Version

1) Since there seems (as someone posted earlier, I think) to be two
   types of suggestions (one camp wants an "easier" hack, the other
   wants a more difficult hack), why not create an april-fools nethack
   with a super-human character type (S is for Superman, for example)
   and more humorous situations (the Wizard is the mc, the Amulet 
   becomes Mr. Microphone, all the shops are run by the Three Stooges,
   etc.).  This character could be made invulnerable ("The flames of
   the dragon tickle you", "The xan tries to prick you but breaks its
   stinger and dies", "You blow all of the monsters against the wall
   and crush them" (Super#breathe), "You munch on the rocks 
   contendedly", etc.) to everything except the piles of gold which
   have been contaminated with kryptonite radiation.  

   I know, it's a hokey idea, but maybe it would satisfy those who need
   a super-character off the bat to boost their egos :-).

2) I thought of an analog to the (G)nome/(G)remlin increase in malevolence.
   Why not have Keystone (K)ops become dete(K)tives in the lower 
   levels?  dete(K)tives would be fewer in number, they would be more
   powerful (with overcoats (AC=9), detective badges, and Boots of 
   Stealth, perhaps) and would mumble things like "Where were you on
   the night of the twelfth, <Character's name>?"

3) Another analog might be having the Witches of Endor appear somewhere
   below the Stooges and above the mazes.  They would have (and use)
   various wands as well as Witch-hats which give the wearer (but not
   the Witch?) invisibility, stealth, charm-monster and polymorph
  (as spells).  They might also have the ability to recharge wands and
   spells if conquered but not slain by the character (they would never
   yield if all three were in the same room).

4) To relieve some of the tedium of either dungeon levels or mazes,
   how about creating large caverns (with stalagtites and stalagmites, 
   pools and chasms) or jail-cell rows (monsters lining both sides of
   a single corridor but held by their cell doors (locked)).
                                                              
5) And, to enhance an idea presented earlier, the character of the
   Alchemist:

>  4)  Or maybe it is time to introduce a new character type:  the
>      Alchemist.  He/she could be equipped with a lab-kit, several
>      potions (identified), a bunsen-burner, a lab-coat (AC 10),
>      special goggles, tongs, gloves, mirror, empty test-tubes,
>      powdered chemicals, water, wielding a beaker of acid (40+).  
>      He/she would have the ability to actually create potions or
>      combine/transform them...

   perhaps the Alchemist could synthesize gems by combining potions
   in his Cauldron and heating them over his Bunsen burner.  The 
   wielded beaker of acid (40+ throws) could supplant the need for
   the Archeologist by being able to eat through rock.  (Naturally,
   the Lab coat protects the Alchemist from acid-splashes).

6) This isn't really a suggestion, but a repeat of a question:  why 
   isn't it possible to set fires (or use fire) other than as a Dragon
   or spell/wand - wielding magic user?  I liked the idea of the
   torches ensconced in the walls of lit rooms, presented earlier.
   Perhaps those torches could be set to last only a certain number
   of turns, burning out at some point (or burning the hand of the
   person who holds it past the point of "That torch is getting pretty
   short").

   Anyway, these are just ideas for discussion.

